course: dictionary
lesson: 1080
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word boy has more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one. «A boy in Halifax squints at the board and sits closer and closer.» Squints, board and glasses are the clues here. Boy means a male child.
explain: Some words say how someone feels. «Boy!» or «Oh boy!» is said to show surprise or excitement, not to name a person. Ask yourself: is this word naming someone, or showing a feeling?
explain: Be careful with boy said to a grown man. «Oi, boy, get over here» is rude, because it treats a grown man like a child. Context tells you it is an insult, not a kind word.
explain: Words from other places work the same way. In Scotland a friend might say «laddie», and in Wales or Ireland «boyo», both friendly words for a boy. When a word is new, check the clues in the sentence first, then use a dictionary.
fact: A boy is a male child or a young man.
fact: «Boy!» or «Oh boy!» shows surprise or excitement, mostly in the USA.
fact: «The boys» means a group of male friends, as in «out with the boys».
fact: «Good boy» is a friendly thing to say to a dog.
fact: In exams and forms, boy may be written as «male pupil», «a male child» or «juvenile».
exercise: «A boy in Halifax squints at the board and sits closer and closer.» What does boy mean in this sentence? | A dog that is lost | A big ship in a harbour | *A male child who needs glasses | A grown man who is ill
exercise: Lucy shouts «Oh boy!» when she wins a prize. What does it show? | Anger about a lost game | A need for a drink | Sleepiness | *Surprise or excitement
exercise: Someone says «mummy's boy» to tease a boy. What does it mean? | *A boy who is very close to his mum | A boy who is very tall | A boy from Scotland | A boy who has a new bike
test: «Out with the boys» means going out with what? | The team coach | Two boys from a school | *A group of male friends | Every person in the class
test: Which friendly word for a boy would a friend in Wales use? | servo | dreich | *boyo | laddie
exam: Which phrase is used on exam forms for a boy? | boy scout | good boy | oh boy | *male pupil
